From 1cbb65a8204ca8f23b8f56f6caedd37cdd801731 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 09:52:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let vendors directly schedule meetings and send calendar
 invites by mail
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a new schedule-meeting-direct edge function so a vendor can put a
meeting straight to "scheduled" from a buyer's detail page — title, date,
duration, join link, and notes — instead of only confirming a buyer-
initiated request. On submit it downloads a real .ics calendar invite and
opens a mailto: draft to the buyer (no transactional email provider is
configured, so sending is a client-side handoff, not a backend relay). Both
the vendor meetings list and the buyer handoff page now show the join link,
duration, and notes, with their own "download .ics" action.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BZibWYPysw75xiFQpbHszf
